# Dependency-Aware Plan

Planning material does not authorize work or external actions.

In Minimal, this file may own individual plan items. In Standard and
High-Assurance, `../machine-readable/plan.json` owns plan-item records and this
file owns planning method, dependency explanation, and summary.

No project-specific plan has been accepted. Build the first plan only after
requirements, current state, findings, risks, and approval gates are inspected.

`depends_on` is the hard `PLAN-####` precedence graph. Readiness is derived,
not stored: a planned item is on the ready frontier only when every predecessor
is completed, every gate is passed or waived, each structured blocker is
resolved, and its acceptance and expected-evidence contracts are populated.
When structured plan items are present, execution tasks link reciprocally
through `task_refs` and `plan_item_refs`; Minimal can derive its executable
frontier from the task graph while retaining plan explanation in Markdown.

Calendar dates may record evidence freshness, gate expiry, or a genuine
external constraint. They never satisfy a dependency, place an item on the
ready frontier, or choose among independent ready items. When several items
are ready, current operator direction or an accepted priority/value/risk
decision supplies the selection basis.
